body: "## Static release-identity mismatch\nPR #67 head `321403235af39961d85a333be0c51120481dda84` prepares version `2026.10.29` in package.json, root lock metadata and manifest.json, but the actual default extension export still declares `2026.10.5` in both [index.ts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/blob/321403235af39961d85a333be0c51120481dda84/index.ts#L2469-L2475) and [committed dist/index.js](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/blob/321403235af39961d85a333be0c51120481dda84/dist/index.js#L1919-L1925).\n\nThe release diff updates the preceding comment's example `version: \"2026.10.28\"` to `.29`, not the actual exported property.\n\n## Exact mechanism and bounded reproduction\n[Release preparation, line153](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/blob/321403235af39961d85a333be0c51120481dda84/.github/workflows/release.yml#L153) uses a non-global first-match replacement:\n```js\nsource.replace(/version:\\s*[\"'][^\"']+[\"']/, 'version: \"' + version + '\"')\n```\nThe first matching text is in the comment describing that replacement. A pure Node string-transform check using this public source excerpt, restoring only the comment's prior `.28` value and applying the exact regex with target `.29`, changes the comment while the export remains `2026.10.5`. Two assertions passed. No repository module, workflow, provider or native tracker was executed.\n\n## Intended contract / impact\n[Canonical release-readiness record pm-jev-release-gate](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/blob/321403235af39961d85a333be0c51120481dda84/.agents/pm/chores/pm-jev-release-gate.toon), delivered by #51, requires verified metadata and packed release contents. The source itself describes the extension identity as release-managed.\n\nConsumers inspecting the exported module receive a stale version inconsistent with the package/manifest, undermining reliable version attribution and diagnostics. Actual host display/cache behavior, installed package behavior and npm publication have **not** been tested or inferred. This is source/committed-output evidence, not a claim that this candidate is published.\n\nAll-status67issues/PRs and canonical issue/chore records checked. Existing #62 / #63 concern tarball argument resolution, not this identity mismatch. PR67 is the current candidate.\n\n## Acceptance / regression\n1. Update the actual exported identity structurally or from a single verified version source; do not match comments/string examples as code.\n2. Fail release preparation when package, manifest and actual source/built default-export versions disagree.\n3. Include a regression with a misleading version literal in a preceding comment and multiple unrelated version strings; check the exported property, not mere text presence.\n4. Verify the packed artifact's actual extension export matches its package/manifest, without executing activation or contacting live providers.\n5. Preserve approval/publishing guards and existing coverage thresholds; no release or credential change is requested by this issue."
